\newlabel{tab:primary}{{2}{8}{Frozen external results at $W=1280$, five paths per graph. PageRank uses a 20-node pool and default solver tolerance. Loss is normalized by full-reference spread beyond the five seeds. Degree agreement is ordered-trajectory agreement}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {5.2}Ranking precision changes one apparent budget reversal}{9}{subsection.5.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Post-hoc PageRank loss across budgets. Each entry is the mean incremental-loss percentage across five original paths at $W=80/320/1280$. Default uses NetworkX tolerance $10^{-6}$; strict uses $10^{-12}$, whose pool is unchanged at $10^{-14}$. Pool Jaccard compares default and strict candidates. This is a numerical sensitivity analysis, not a new primary test family.}}{9}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:precision-budget}{{3}{9}{Post-hoc PageRank loss across budgets. Each entry is the mean incremental-loss percentage across five original paths at $W=80/320/1280$. Default uses NetworkX tolerance $10^{-6}$; strict uses $10^{-12}$, whose pool is unchanged at $10^{-14}$. Pool Jaccard compares default and strict candidates. This is a numerical sensitivity analysis, not a new primary test family}{table.3}{}}
